| Post-image blob hashes | Makefile `b8f816215f6cc567` · `dalvik_engine.cpp` `739cfd1efb517f26` · `android_shadows.cpp` `7d8375c900883ec7` · `r25_dispatch_matrix_test.cpp` `bf39053b9f569c36` |
| Gates (this lane's sandbox) | full build green `make -j1` · smoke PASS · `make test` **4/4** · `mwr_opcode_probe` **5/5** · `r25_matrix` **14/14** · APK battery BLOCKED (no javac/aapt2/d8 — no behavior claim, no honesty-gate relaxation) |

PART 1/3 below (`miniandroid/src/dex/dalvik_engine.cpp`). Apply parts 1+2+3 in order on a clean `14c4bf4e`.

<details><summary>PATCH PART 1/3</summary>

```diff
diff --git a/miniandroid/src/dex/dalvik_engine.cpp b/miniandroid/src/dex/dalvik_engine.cpp
index e1078a06..739cfd1e 100755
--- a/miniandroid/src/dex/dalvik_engine.cpp
+++ b/miniandroid/src/dex/dalvik_engine.cpp
@@ -2897,13 +2897,53 @@ std::string DalvikExecutionEngine::resolve_method_proto_uncached(
 fallback:
     // Fallback: try the merged DexReport's method_ids + protos tables.
     if (dex_report_ && method_idx < dex_report_->method_ids.size()) {
-        uint16_t proto_idx = dex_report_->method_ids[method_idx].proto_idx;
-        (void)proto_idx;
-        // We can't reliably resolve proto_idx via the merged protos vector
-        // because multi-DEX merging shifts indices. Return an empty
-        // descriptor so the caller (execute_invoke_static) treats this as
-        // a no-arg method (which is the safe default for $r8$lambda methods
-        // where the proto is used only for wide-register merging decisions).
+        // ── A-R5 (S218, V2 fix — R25 matrix wave): CLASS-INFO PROTO
+        // FALLBACK LAW. The old fallback returned the CONSTANT "()V" —
+        // even though the method's TRUE descriptor is sitting in the
+        // merged class-info tables (method_ids[method_idx] →
+        // (class_idx, name_idx) → class_info_index_ → the class's
+        // direct/virtual method entry). The constant leaked into every
+        // descriptor-sensitive decision: the F-280 exact-(name, proto)
+        // match (dalvik_engine.cpp, the F-280 block inside
+        // try_recursive_invoke) compared "()V" against the real "()I"
+        // and declared NO local match → its super-walk let an ANCESTOR's
+        // lenient-selected same-name body outrank the receiver's own
+        // declaration (the R25 dispatch-matrix probe's v_declared_super
+        // row: new LSub; + invoke-virtual LBase.m answered 1, the base
+        // body, instead of the override's 2 — the exact ART-law
+        // violation §5 C3 demanded the matrix surface). First
+        // observable: tests/r25_dispatch_matrix_test.cpp rows at
+        // 14c4bf4e + /tmp dbg minimal repro (new-instance LSub; +
+        // invoke-virtual (LSub.m) → LBase.m body ran).
+        // Fix: consult the class-info method tables BEFORE the constant
+        // default; first same-name non-empty descriptor wins (overload
+        // ambiguity documented — best-available, strictly more accurate
+        // than the constant; the raw-DEX path above is untouched so
+        // real-APK proto_ids resolution is byte-identical).
+        uint16_t class_idx = dex_report_->method_ids[method_idx].class_idx;
+        uint32_t name_idx = dex_report_->method_ids[method_idx].name_idx;
+        if (class_idx < dex_report_->types.size() &&
+            name_idx < dex_report_->strings.size()) {
+            const std::string& cname = dex_report_->types[class_idx];
+            const std::string& mname = dex_report_->strings[name_idx];
+            auto cit = class_info_index_.find(cname);
+            if (!cname.empty() && !mname.empty() &&
+                cit != class_info_index_.end()) {
+                const dex::ClassInfo& ci =
+                    dex_report_->classes[cit->second];
+                for (const auto& mm : ci.direct_methods)
+                    if (mm.name == mname && !mm.descriptor.empty())
+                        return mm.descriptor;
+                for (const auto& mm : ci.virtual_methods)
+                    if (mm.name == mname && !mm.descriptor.empty())
+                        return mm.descriptor;
+            }
+        }
+        // (The raw proto_idx route stays the raw-DEX path above; the merged
+        // protos vector cannot be used because multi-DEX merging shifts indices.)
+        // because multi-DEX merging shifts indices. After the class-info
+        // consult above, the "()V" constant remains only for methods that
+        // exist in NO class-info table (merged-away classes).
     }
     return "()V";
 }
@@ -51427,6 +51467,205 @@ bool DalvikExecutionEngine::bridge_to_api(const std::string& class_name,
             result = DalvikValue::make_bool(cur.empty());
             return true;
         }
+        // ── A-R5 (S218, R24 delivery): the AbstractStringBuilder MUTATION
+        // family. Finding R24 (issue #581, A-R4): the SB block handled only
+        // append/toString/length/charAt/isEmpty and its own boundary comment
+        // deferred the rest. The deferred half is NOT inert: setLength(0) —
+        // the universal HUD/score-text reset idiom that game loops run per
+        // frame — fell to the typed-void tail, so the buffer kept its old
+        // content and every append ACCUMULATED (frame N's text = the
+        // concatenation of frames 1..N): the silent-wrong class
+        // CONSTITUTION_V2 §17 forbids, reached through one of the most
+        // common idioms in game UI code.
+        //
+        // Law (Tier 1, OpenJDK AbstractStringBuilder):
+        //   insert(int, X)       — shifts the tail; StringIndexOutOfBounds
+        //                          when offset < 0 or > length;
+        //   setLength(int)       — truncates (newLength < length) or
+        //                          zero-fills (NUL chars); negative is
+        //                          StringIndexOutOfBoundsException;
+        //   setCharAt(int, char) — bounds law identical to charAt;
+        //   delete(int, int)     — clamps end to length; start > end or
+        //                          start > length is StringIndexOutOfBounds;
+        //   deleteCharAt(int)    — StringIndexOutOfBounds outside
+        //                          [0, length);
+        //   reverse()            — reverses in place (UTF-16 units — this
+        //                          runtime stores UTF-8 bytes in sb_value;
+        //                          the byte reversal is the documented
+        //                          approximation, surrogate-pair exactness
+        //                          is the follow-up lever);
+        //   replace(int,int,Str) — start/end bounds per delete law;
+        //   substring(int[,int]) — bounds law; returns the slice;
+        //   capacity()/ensureCapacity/trimToSize — implementation-defined;
+        //   capacity() answers max(16, length+16) (the informational
+        //   minimum-capacity law face, no new state).
+        //   The mutating faces return `this` (chaining law, same shape as
+        //   the append arm); the bounds laws throw_deferred
+        //   StringIndexOutOfBoundsException with the exact OpenJDK message
+        //   shapes.
+        {
+            auto r24_writeback = [&](const std::string& v) {
+                if (sb_id != 0 && heap_.has_object(sb_id))
+                    heap_.set_object_field(sb_id, "sb_value",
+                                           DalvikValue::make_string(v, 0));
+            };
+            auto r24_int_arg = [&](size_t i) -> int32_t {
+                return dalvik_int_value(args[i]);
+            };
+            auto r24_this = [&]() {
+                status = ApiCallTrace::Status::IMPLEMENTED;
+                DalvikValue r;
+                r.type = DalvikType::OBJECT_REF;
+                r.object_id = sb_id;
+                r.class_desc = class_name.c_str();
+                result = r;
+                return true;
+            };
+            auto r24_sioobe = [&](const std::string& msg) {
+                throw_deferred("Ljava/lang/StringIndexOutOfBoundsException;",
+                               msg, "R24-SB");
+                result = DalvikValue::make_null();
+                status = ApiCallTrace::Status::IMPLEMENTED;
+                return true;
+            };
+
+            if (method == "setLength" && args.size() >= 2 &&
+                args[1].type == DalvikType::INT32) {
+                int32_t nl = r24_int_arg(1);
+                if (nl < 0)
+                    return r24_sioobe("length " + std::to_string(nl) +
+                                      " < 0");
+                if (static_cast<size_t>(nl) <= cur.size())
+                    cur.resize(static_cast<size_t>(nl));
+                else
+                    cur.append(static_cast<size_t>(nl) - cur.size(), '\0');
+                r24_writeback(cur);
+                status = ApiCallTrace::Status::IMPLEMENTED;
+                result = DalvikValue::make_void();
+                return true;
+            }
+            if (method == "setCharAt" && args.size() >= 3 &&
+                args[1].type == DalvikType::INT32) {
+                int32_t idx = r24_int_arg(1);
+                if (idx < 0 || static_cast<size_t>(idx) >= cur.size())
+                    return r24_sioobe("index " + std::to_string(idx) +
+                                      ", length " +
+                                      std::to_string(cur.size()));
+                char c = 0;
+                if (args[2].type == DalvikType::CHAR ||
+                    args[2].type == DalvikType::INT32)
+                    c = static_cast<char>(args[2].int_val);
+                cur[static_cast<size_t>(idx)] = c;
+                r24_writeback(cur);
+                status = ApiCallTrace::Status::IMPLEMENTED;
+                result = DalvikValue::make_void();
+                return true;
+            }
+            if (method == "insert" && args.size() >= 3 &&
+                args[1].type == DalvikType::INT32) {
+                int32_t idx = r24_int_arg(1);
+                if (idx < 0 || static_cast<size_t>(idx) > cur.size())
+                    return r24_sioobe("offset " + std::to_string(idx) +
+                                      ", length " +
+                                      std::to_string(cur.size()));
+                cur.insert(static_cast<size_t>(idx),
+                           stringify_arg(args[2]));
+                r24_writeback(cur);
+                return r24_this();
+            }
+            if (method == "deleteCharAt" && args.size() >= 2 &&
+                args[1].type == DalvikType::INT32) {
+                int32_t idx = r24_int_arg(1);
+                if (idx < 0 || static_cast<size_t>(idx) >= cur.size())
+                    return r24_sioobe("index " + std::to_string(idx) +
+                                      ", length " +
+                                      std::to_string(cur.size()));
+                cur.erase(static_cast<size_t>(idx), 1);
+                r24_writeback(cur);
+                return r24_this();
+            }
+            if (method == "delete" && args.size() >= 3 &&
+                args[1].type == DalvikType::INT32 &&
+                args[2].type == DalvikType::INT32) {
+                int32_t start = r24_int_arg(1), end = r24_int_arg(2);
+                if (end > static_cast<int32_t>(cur.size()))
+                    end = static_cast<int32_t>(cur.size());
+                if (start < 0 || start > end ||
+                    start > static_cast<int32_t>(cur.size()))
+                    return r24_sioobe("start " + std::to_string(start) +
+                                      ", end " + std::to_string(end) +
+                                      ", length " +
+                                      std::to_string(cur.size()));
+                cur.erase(static_cast<size_t>(start),
+                          static_cast<size_t>(end - start));
+                r24_writeback(cur);
+                return r24_this();
+            }
+            if (method == "reverse") {
+                std::reverse(cur.begin(), cur.end());
+                r24_writeback(cur);
+                return r24_this();
+            }
+            if (method == "replace" && args.size() >= 4 &&
+                args[1].type == DalvikType::INT32 &&
+                args[2].type == DalvikType::INT32) {
+                int32_t start = r24_int_arg(1), end = r24_int_arg(2);
+                if (end > static_cast<int32_t>(cur.size()))
+                    end = static_cast<int32_t>(cur.size());
+                if (start < 0 || start > end ||
+                    start > static_cast<int32_t>(cur.size()))
+                    return r24_sioobe("start " + std::to_string(start) +
+                                      ", end " + std::to_string(end) +
+                                      ", length " +
+                                      std::to_string(cur.size()));
+                cur.replace(static_cast<size_t>(start),
+                            static_cast<size_t>(end - start),
+                            stringify_arg(args[3]));
+                r24_writeback(cur);
+                return r24_this();
+            }
+            if (method == "substring" && args.size() >= 2 &&
+                args[1].type == DalvikType::INT32) {
+                int32_t start = r24_int_arg(1);
+                int32_t end = (args.size() >= 3 &&
+                               args[2].type == DalvikType::INT32)
+                                  ? r24_int_arg(2)
+                                  : static_cast<int32_t>(cur.size());
+                if (start < 0 || end > static_cast<int32_t>(cur.size()) ||
+                    start > end)
+                    return r24_sioobe("begin " + std::to_string(start) +
+                                      ", end " + std::to_string(end) +
+                                      ", length " +
+                                      std::to_string(cur.size()));
+                status = ApiCallTrace::Status::IMPLEMENTED;
+                result = DalvikValue::make_string(
+                    cur.substr(static_cast<size_t>(start),
+                               static_cast<size_t>(end - start)),
+                    0);
+                return true;
+            }
+            if (method == "capacity") {
+                // Informational minimum-capacity law face: OpenJDK capacity
+                // is implementation-defined (min 16, grows 2n+2); this
+                // runtime keeps content only, so the answer mirrors the
+                // minimum guaranteed capacity for the current length.
+                status = ApiCallTrace::Status::IMPLEMENTED;
+                result = DalvikValue::make_int(
+                    static_cast<int32_t>(cur.size() + 16 > 16
+                                             ? cur.size() + 16
+                                             : 16));
+                return true;
+            }
+            if (method == "ensureCapacity" ||
+                method == "trimToSize") {
+                // Capacity hints are no-ops here (no separate capacity
+                // state exists); the content is untouched — OpenJDK law:
+                // both may change capacity, never content.
+                status = ApiCallTrace::Status::IMPLEMENTED;
+                result = DalvikValue::make_void();
+                return true;
+            }
+        }
         // insert(int, X), reverse(), deleteCharAt, setLength etc. can be
         // added when evidence shows they're on a hot path.
     }
```
</details>

## The A-R5 patch — PART 2/3 (shadows + Makefile — R23 the Collections algorithmic static face + the two probe targets) — base `14c4bf4e` (current `origin/main` S217 HEAD), sha16 `35e0c189b6d21746`

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Base | `14c4bf4e` (a single `git apply` of parts 1+2+3 in order on a clean tree reproduces the whole delivery) |
| Shape | 4 files, **+1,437 / −7** |
| Patch SHA256 | `35e0c189b6d21746…` (sha256sum sha16 prefix) |
| `git apply --check` | **CLEAN rc=0** on a pristine `14c4bf4e` worktree, verified before posting (per K-2.4) |
| Post-image blob hashes | Makefile `b8f816215f6cc567` · `dalvik_engine.cpp` `739cfd1efb517f26` · `android_shadows.cpp` `7d8375c900883ec7` · `r25_dispatch_matrix_test.cpp` `bf39053b9f569c36` |
| Gates (this lane's sandbox) | full build green `make -j1` · smoke PASS · `make test` **4/4** · `mwr_opcode_probe` **5/5** · `r25_matrix` **14/14** · APK battery BLOCKED (no javac/aapt2/d8 — no behavior claim, no honesty-gate relaxation) |

PART 2/3 below (`miniandroid/src/framework/android_shadows.cpp` + `miniandroid/Makefile`). Apply parts 1+2+3 in order on a clean `14c4bf4e`.

<details><summary>PATCH PART 2/3</summary>

```diff
diff --git a/miniandroid/Makefile b/miniandroid/Makefile
index 617e0bc7..b8f81621 100755
--- a/miniandroid/Makefile
+++ b/miniandroid/Makefile
@@ -163,6 +163,28 @@ $(LAWS130_EXECUTABLE): $(CORE_OBJECTS) $(QUICKJS_OBJECTS) $(LAWS130_SOURCE)
 	@mkdir -p $(BUILDDIR)
 	$(CXX) $(CXXFLAGS) $(INCLUDES) $(JSON_INCLUDE) -o $@ $(LAWS130_SOURCE) $(CORE_OBJECTS) $(QUICKJS_OBJECTS) $(LIBS) $(FONTS_LIBS)

+# A-R5 (S218): the R25 declared≠runtime receiver dispatch matrix probe
+# (roadmap §5 C3's demanded deliverable) + the A-R4 mwr opcode probe —
+# both linked per the LAWS130 pattern (+ THUNK_OBJECT, the S215 receipt's
+# link correction: miniandroid_native_thunk lives in the thunk object).
+MWR_PROBE_SOURCE = $(TESTDIR)/mwr_opcode_probe_test.cpp
+MWR_PROBE_EXECUTABLE = $(BUILDDIR)/mwr_opcode_probe
+mwr_opcode_probe: $(MWR_PROBE_EXECUTABLE)
+	./$(MWR_PROBE_EXECUTABLE)
+
+$(MWR_PROBE_EXECUTABLE): $(CORE_OBJECTS) $(QUICKJS_OBJECTS) $(THUNK_OBJECT) $(MWR_PROBE_SOURCE)
+	@mkdir -p $(BUILDDIR)
+	$(CXX) $(CXXFLAGS) $(INCLUDES) $(JSON_INCLUDE) -o $@ $(MWR_PROBE_SOURCE) $(CORE_OBJECTS) $(QUICKJS_OBJECTS) $(THUNK_OBJECT) $(LIBS) $(FONTS_LIBS)
+
+R25_SOURCE = $(TESTDIR)/r25_dispatch_matrix_test.cpp
+R25_EXECUTABLE = $(BUILDDIR)/r25_dispatch_matrix
+r25_matrix: $(R25_EXECUTABLE)
+	./$(R25_EXECUTABLE)
+
+$(R25_EXECUTABLE): $(CORE_OBJECTS) $(QUICKJS_OBJECTS) $(THUNK_OBJECT) $(R25_SOURCE)
+	@mkdir -p $(BUILDDIR)
+	$(CXX) $(CXXFLAGS) $(INCLUDES) $(JSON_INCLUDE) -o $@ $(R25_SOURCE) $(CORE_OBJECTS) $(QUICKJS_OBJECTS) $(THUNK_OBJECT) $(LIBS) $(FONTS_LIBS)
+
 test: $(TEST_EXECUTABLE)
 	./$(TEST_EXECUTABLE)

diff --git a/miniandroid/src/framework/android_shadows.cpp b/miniandroid/src/framework/android_shadows.cpp
index c93d28ab..7d8375c9 100755
--- a/miniandroid/src/framework/android_shadows.cpp
+++ b/miniandroid/src/framework/android_shadows.cpp
@@ -1183,6 +1183,661 @@ CallResult CollectionShadow::dispatch(const CallContext& ctx) {
             }
             return CallResult::handled_void();
         }
+
+        // ── A-R5 (S218, R23 delivery): the Collections ALGORITHMIC static face ──
+        // Finding R23 (issue #576, A-R1): the engine's only two
+        // Ljava/util/Collections; blocks were the synchronized*/factories
+        // family (dalvik_engine.cpp) and the singleton/empty family
+        // (this block); CollectionShadow::handles_class claimed the class but
+        // its dispatch contained NO algorithmic arm. Every void-returning
+        // algorithmic entry (reverse/shuffle/swap/rotate/fill/copy) fell to
+        // the typed-void tail — THE LIST STAYED UNTRANSFORMED while every
+        // caller believed it mutated (the exact silent-wrong shape W12 closed
+        // for sort; okio Options was its live face). Value-returning entries
+        // (min/max/binarySearch/frequency/…) answered typed defaults.
+        //
+        // Law (Tier 1, OpenJDK java.util.Collections): reverse/shuffle/swap/
+        // rotate/fill/copy mutate the list per the specified contract;
+        // nCopies/addAll produce; min/max/binarySearch are comparator/
+        // Comparable-driven queries with NoSuchElementException (empty) and
+        // ClassCastException (incomparable) contracts; frequency/disjoint/
+        // replaceAll/indexOfSubList/lastIndexOfSubList classify by
+        // Objects.equals (the F-NEW-238/236d equality machinery below).
+        // Machinery reuse: the F-606 static-sort face already proved the
+        // whole shape — arg_as_object takes the list from args[0] on static
+        // calls, the four parallel stores carry elements (kinds 1/2/3/4),
+        // the K14 dex_invoke_slot drives app comparators/compareTo, and the
+        // heap array[i] re-sync keeps dual-store lists coherent.
+        //
+        // Determinism note (the runtime's global determinism law — corpus
+        // goldens are byte-exact): shuffle uses a FIXED-seed splitmix64
+        // stream. OpenJDK seeds shuffle's internal Random from nanoTime —
+        // a nondeterminism this runtime intentionally does NOT reproduce.
+        // Successive shuffles in one process advance the same stream (like
+        // the shared unseeded-Random lane F-C8-170), and the stream resets
+        // per process, so runs stay byte-reproducible.
+        {
+            const auto& r23_dex = CollectionShadow::dex_invoke_slot();
+            const auto& r23_app_eq = CollectionShadow::app_equals_slot();
+
+            // Element count across both store shapes (dense + view).
+            auto r23_n = [](const CollectionShadow::CollectionState* st)
+                -> int32_t {
+                return static_cast<int32_t>(st->elements.size() +
+                                            st->view_elements.size());
+            };
+
+            // Read slot i as a CallContext::Arg (same normalization the
+            // F-606 sort face uses; kind 4 = typed null per F-NEW-271).
+            auto r23_elem = [&](const CollectionShadow::CollectionState* st,
+                                int32_t i) -> CallContext::Arg {
+                CallContext::Arg a;
+                if (!st->view_elements.empty()) {
+                    const auto& ve = st->view_elements[i];
+                    if (ve.kind == 4) a.kind = CallContext::Arg::Kind::NULL_REF;
+                    else if (ve.kind == 3) { a.kind = CallContext::Arg::Kind::INT; a.int_val = ve.int_val; }
+                    else if (ve.kind == 2) { a.kind = CallContext::Arg::Kind::STRING; a.string_val = ve.string_val; }
+                    else { a.kind = CallContext::Arg::Kind::OBJECT; a.object_id = ve.object_id; }
+                    return a;
+                }
+                uint32_t oid = i < (int32_t)st->elements.size() ? st->elements[i] : 0;
+                uint8_t k = i < (int32_t)st->elem_kinds.size()
+                                ? st->elem_kinds[i] : (oid ? 1 : 2);
+                if (k == 4) a.kind = CallContext::Arg::Kind::NULL_REF;
+                else if (k == 3 && i < (int32_t)st->elem_ints.size()) { a.kind = CallContext::Arg::Kind::INT; a.int_val = st->elem_ints[i]; }
+                else if (k == 2 && i < (int32_t)st->elem_strings.size()) { a.kind = CallContext::Arg::Kind::STRING; a.string_val = st->elem_strings[i]; }
+                else { a.kind = CallContext::Arg::Kind::OBJECT; a.object_id = oid; }
+                return a;
+            };
+
+            // Classify an Arg into the (item, kind, ival, sval) store tuple
+            // (same law as lawb_classify_arg: int-family → 3, string → 2,
+            // object → 1, null/zero-ref → 4).
+            auto r23_classify = [](const CallContext::Arg& a, uint32_t& item,
+                                   uint8_t& kind, int32_t& ival,
+                                   std::string& sval) {
